WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.102
-Our next guest is a
talented actress and comedian

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:04.904
you know from shows like
"Search Party"

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.372
and "What We Do in the Shadows,"

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:09.075
and movies such as "Dating in
New York" and "The Lovebirds."

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.978
Her new special,
"The Twist? She's Gorgeous,"

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:14.080
begins streaming on Netflix
March 15.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.081
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.849
-I hate the summer.

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.251
All I've ever done in a bikini
is sob.

00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:20.386
[ Audience laughs ]

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.955
But one thing I love about
summer,

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:24.690
[chuckles] I have to say,

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:28.227
is those hot,
hot summer anthems.

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:32.398
So if the DJ could just drop
that track real quick,

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:33.399
that'd be sick.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:34.533
[ Upbeat piano music plays ]

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:38.137
I'm really more of a dancer
than a comedian.

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:40.773
Dancer first, choreographer
second, model third,

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:42.841
comedian fourth.

00:00:42.841 --> 00:00:44.844
-Please welcome back to
the show, our friend,

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.345
Catherine Cohen.

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:49.348
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:54.921 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:54.921 --> 00:01:00.459 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:01.694
Welcome back.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:04.263
-Oh, my God, I'm so happy
to be back, finally.

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:07.600
-It's been -- it's weirdly
not as long --

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.236
or it's longer than I feel like
it's been since you were here.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.472
-Well, I told my parents I was
coming on the show and my dad

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.907
was like, "Wow, I can't believe
we get to go to Seth Meyers

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.141
twice in one year."

00:01:16.141 --> 00:01:17.510
And I said, "That was
three years ago, babe."

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.912
-[ Laughs ] Yeah, it's been
a weird three years.

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:20.947
-I know.
-In his defense,

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.315
it's been a weird three years.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.018
-I've loved it. No, it's been
absolute hell on Earth.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.685
-Well, you know, it's
interesting because

00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:28.988
you did a song, "Look at Me,"
which is the opening song

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.256
in the special.
-Yes.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.091
-And I should -- you have
a beautiful singing voice.

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:33.626
This is incredible musical
comedy.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:34.994
-Stop, stop.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:37.096
-Seth, you're embarrassing me.

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:39.465
-But you -- this is the opening
song in your special.

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.033
So obviously, you've had a lot
of this material

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.801
for a long time because this is
a special that was supposed

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:45.238
to tape when the pandemic
happened, so it must be

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.672
so thrilling to have it
coming out.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:48.207
-Truly, it's a dream come true.
-Yeah.

00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:49.541
-I'm so psyched.

00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:51.777
-And this is such a unique
to New York style of show,

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.313
this cabaret comedy show.
-Yes!

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.814
-What have -- [ Laughs ]
Yeah.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.916
I'm about -- I'm really plugged
in to New York, so I know --

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.150
-[Laughing] I know, right?

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.452
-And what was it like when
Netflix called and said,

00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:02.589
"We want to do this kind of show
for a standup special?"

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.391
-Well, [laughs] When they --
I've been working on the show

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.860
for many years.
I do a weekly show

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.394
at Club Cumming
in the East village.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.630
I did the Edinburgh Fringe,
which I know, you know and love.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.964
-Yes, the best.
-The best, the best.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:15.901
And then I hurt my vocal cords
and I couldn't talk for,

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.337
like, two months.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:20.406
So when Netflix called to tell
me I was going to get a special,

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.741
they told me the news and I
literally couldn't say a word.

00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:24.777
I was on vocal rest.
I was like...

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.345
[ Laughs ]

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:28.014
-Feverishly clapping the phone.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:30.049
On the other line they're like,
"OK, well, bye.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.418
Like, reach out."

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.254
But then I was, you know,
physically very excited.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.557
-You've been doing this a long
time -- as you mentioned,

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:40.126
working on this show a long
time, and this is very unique

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.361
for us. You and Patty,
our previous guest,

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:44.430
worked together over the years.
-Stop!

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.499
-This is a sketch you did?

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.968
-Yeah, it's highbrow art,
performance art.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.436
-OK, and what is the name --

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.637
what would you call
this sketch?

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:54.140
-This was called Slurp.
It was about two girlies

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.508
just rubbing ice cream
all over their faces.

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:57.509
-[ Laughs ]
-It's kind of probably over

00:02:57.509 --> 00:02:59.412
your head, so I don't --
-Yeah, no.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.280
I think without the context,
we're all like, "Wow."

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.881
But I think most of us
want to see it.

00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:05.518
-Absolutely.
It's out there in the cloud.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.886
Yeah.
-So you grew up in Texas.

00:03:07.886 --> 00:03:10.322
You attended Christian schools.

00:03:10.322 --> 00:03:13.559
Are people thrown by the path
you've chosen to take?

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:16.429
-I know, because I became
an absolute wretched slut, yeah.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.864
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.666
No, I --
-Which is, like, the one thing.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:21.400
It was, like, they had that in
Latin.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.002
Don't do that.
-That's what they always said.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.937
No, my dad's Jewish,
my mom's Catholic.

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:28.308
I went to these Christian
schools, and then I just got,

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:30.143
like, too horny and I left.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.143
-Yeah.

00:03:31.143 --> 00:03:32.245
-I left it all behind.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.480
-Was that, like, sort of
a mutual split?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.915
Did they sort of
also appreciate it?

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.583
They're like,
"New York might better."

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.218
-I think, yeah, this
is a much better fit.

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:40.386
Yeah, but there you go.

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:43.522
-Part of what makes your
stage show so compelling

00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:44.924
is it's incredibly honest.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.892
Are there, though, things
that you do on stage,

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:49.595
maybe things in the special,
that you were on the fence about

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:50.796
whether or not you wanted
to include?

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:52.164
-Oh, so many things.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:52.164 --> 00:03:54.233
-We'll find out tomorrow
what the verdict is.

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:57.136
You know, I have a story about
-- how do I put this?

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.638
I'm a very romantic woman.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:01.874
I need to send a picture of
my crotch to, you know, lovers,

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.676
doctors, that kind of thing.
-Right, right.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.810
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:06.412
-And so I was taking a photo
of my crotch

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.380
and I didn't realize
that I was on selfie mode.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.317
And so in the background,
I saw my face just complete --

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.985
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:14.786
Dead-eyed. You know when you
accidentally take a selfie,

00:04:14.786 --> 00:04:16.388
and it's just like --
-Right.

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:17.957
-It's a harrowing moment.

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.725
-Well, it's harrowing because
you realize

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:21.927
that's how most people see
your face all the time.

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.596
-Nonstop.
I mean, yeah, look at it, yeah.

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.031
-Yeah.
-Totally.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:27.533
So that made the cut, so yeah.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.668
More where that came from.
More gold.

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:33.106
-You're doing Netflix is a Joke,
it's a festival.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.173
-Yes.
-This spring.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.642
That's so exciting.
-I'm so excited.

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:37.543
-You're also doing shows
in Los Angeles.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:39.378
I would say, "tell people
where to get tickets,"

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:40.546
but I've also heard
it's sold out.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:43.149
-Stop. I love that.
That's great news.

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:44.951
-Well, I heard it
via your people.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:45.952
-I told you that, yeah.

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:46.986
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:49.288
I was like, "I don't know
if that's true."

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:51.390
I'm like, "Well, Seth,
it's sold out."

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.859
No, I'm psyched.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.694
-It must be so great.
And I would only imagine

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:57.163
it's going to be so exciting
to do material

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.497
after people see this special.

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:00.465
-Yes.
-Is there then this pressure

00:05:00.465 --> 00:05:01.934
to have new stuff?
-Absolutely.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.302
I'm working on a new hour.

00:05:03.302 --> 00:05:04.737
The old jokes feel very old.

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:08.073
I feel like having, you know,
two years of waiting to tape it,

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:11.110
I ended up having to listen to
an old recording of myself

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.345
to remember my jokes, and I was
like, "Who's that girl?

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:14.847
She sounds fabulous."

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:16.115
I was like, "My brain is broken.

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.216
I don't know what any of that
is anymore."

00:05:18.216 --> 00:05:19.385
But we got back there.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.053
-Well, I'm very happy
that it's available

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:22.655
for everybody to see.
-Oh, I'm so happy.

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:23.889
-And it is so nice to have you
back on the show.

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:25.190
Thank you for making time
for us.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:26.558
-Thank you so much.
It's truly a dream come true.

00:05:26.558 --> 00:05:28.561
-You guys,
that's Catherine Cohen!

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:31.764
"The Twist? She's Gorgeous"
is streaming tomorrow

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:34.466
on Netflix, and
Netflix is a Joke, the festival,

00:05:34.466 --> 00:05:36.368
begins April 28th
in Los Angeles.

00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:37.904
We'll be right back with more
"Late Night."

